### Cleanup a user's groups

Remove the specified user from the specified user groups (only the memberships are removed; the groups themselves are not deleted). Unlike the full asynchronous `cleanup/users/permission/` cleanup, this API executes **synchronously** and returns the result group by group, so the caller can verify the actual cleanup result.

Before cleanup, use `subjects/user/{subject_id}/groups/` to list the groups the user has joined and their `id` values, which can be used as `group_ids` here; after cleanup, verify the records via the audit events API (`audits/events/`, `type=group.member.delete`, `username` is the cleaned user).

#### Parameters

| Field | Type | Location | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| username | string | body | yes | Username |
| group_ids | array[int] | body | yes | Group ID list, at most 100 (duplicates included); duplicate IDs are deduplicated automatically |

#### Request

```json
{
  "username": "zhangsan",
  "group_ids": [1001, 1002]
}
```

#### Response

> Status: 200 OK

```json
{
  "code": 0,
  "message": "OK",
  "data": {
    "removed": [1001],
    "failed": [1002]
  }
}
```

Field notes:

- `removed`: IDs of the groups whose removal succeeded. Note that this field means "the removal call succeeded": groups the user does not belong to (including repeated calls) are also included; it does not mean the membership was actually deleted
- `failed`: IDs of the groups whose removal failed (e.g. backend call errors); a failure for one group does not affect the others
